time=2026-10-17T00:23:08.651Z level=INFO msg="model prompt" record=prov-2026-81333e45 attempt=1 prompt="## The change\n\nSession helpers for commands that need a Provisio session (blueprint prov-2026-ee401a6a, section 4), cmd/provenance/session_run.go. Local commands never call them and never read the credential store or the network (cmd/provenance/auth_offline_test.go). exitError carries a process exit status; exitCode(err) is 3 for it when code is 3 and 1 for any other error; sessionError maps auth.ErrNoSession, ErrSessionExpired and ErrTokenRejected to exit status 3 with the exact messages in the constants; sessionManager reads the server from PROVISIO_AUTH_URL, else from the stored credential, else the default; withSession(ctx, fn) is what publish, clone and import (M4) call. Also main.go: its main() is rendered by the cobra generator package (template cmd/{bin}/main.go): it exits with the status of the first error that has an ExitCode() int method, else 1, so exitError needs ExitCode() and main.go carries no hand edit.\n\nFile cmd/provenance/session_run.go (go package, package main). Imports, each its own addImport, exactly these: context, errors, os, path/filepath, time, github.com/livecodelife/provenance/auth.\n\nDeclarations, in this order, each exactly one set* call (file kwarg cmd/provenance/session_run.go) whose code kwarg is the code below verbatim (gofmt-formatted, comments kept). Do not alter, reorder or add anything. A const or var group is one setConst or setVar named after its first name; setMethod takes receiver and name separately.\n\n  - setType name exitError, code exactly:\n      // exitError carries a process exit status for main to use.\n      type exitError struct {\n      \tcode int\n      \terr  error\n      }\n  - setMethod receiver exitError name Error, code exactly:\n      func (e *exitError) Error() string { return e.err.Error() }\n  - setMethod receiver exitError name Unwrap, code exactly:\n      func (e *exitError) Unwrap() error { return e.err }\n  - setMethod receiver exitError name ExitCode, code exactly:\n      // ExitCode is the status main exits with (the generated main looks for it).\n      func (e *exitError) ExitCode() int { return e.code }\n  - setFunction name exitCode, code exactly:\n      // exitCode is the process exit status for err: 3 when a Provisio session is\n      // needed or has expired, 1 for anything else.\n      func exitCode(err error) int {\n      \tvar ee *exitError\n      \tif errors.As(err, &ee) {\n      \t\treturn ee.code\n      \t}\n      \treturn 1\n      }\n  - setConst name msgNeedSession, code exactly:\n      const (\n      \tmsgNeedSession   = \"This command needs a Provisio session. Run provenance login (or set PROVISIO_TOKEN in CI).\"\n      \tmsgSessionExpire = \"Your Provisio session has expired. Run provenance login.\"\n      \tmsgTokenRejected = \"The personal token was rejected (revoked or expired). Replace PROVISIO_TOKEN, or run provenance login.\"\n      )\n  - setFunction name sessionError, code exactly:\n      // sessionError turns an auth failure into the user-facing message with exit\n      // status 3; other errors pass through unchanged.\n      func sessionError(err error) error {\n      \tswitch {\n      \tcase err == nil:\n      \t\treturn nil\n      \tcase errors.Is(err, auth.ErrNoSession):\n      \t\treturn &exitError{3, errors.New(msgNeedSession)}\n      \tcase errors.Is(err, auth.ErrSessionExpired):\n      \t\treturn &exitError{3, errors.New(msgSessionExpire)}\n      \tcase errors.Is(err, auth.ErrTokenRejected):\n      \t\treturn &exitError{3, errors.New(msgTokenRejected)}\n      \t}\n      \treturn err\n      }\n  - setFunction name serverURL, code exactly:\n      // serverURL is the auth service for a new sign-in: PROVISIO_AUTH_URL, else the\n      // default. Commands that use a stored sign-in prefer the server it was made on.\n      func serverURL() string {\n      \tif s := os.Getenv(auth.EnvServer); s != \"\" {\n      \t\treturn s\n      \t}\n      \treturn auth.DefaultServer\n      }\n  - setFunction name sessionManager, code exactly:\n      // sessionManager builds the token manager over the default credential store.\n      func sessionManager() (*auth.Manager, error) {\n      \tstore, err := auth.DefaultStore()\n      \tif err != nil {\n      \t\treturn nil, err\n      \t}\n      \tpath, err := auth.DefaultFilePath()\n      \tif err != nil {\n      \t\treturn nil, err\n      \t}\n      \tserver := serverURL()\n      \tif os.Getenv(auth.EnvServer) == \"\" && os.Getenv(auth.EnvToken) == \"\" {\n      \t\tif cred, _, err := store.Load(); err == nil && cred.Server != \"\" {\n      \t\t\tserver = cred.Server\n      \t\t}\n      \t}\n      \treturn &auth.Manager{\n      \t\tStore:    store,\n      \t\tClient:   &auth.Client{Server: server},\n      \t\tLockPath: filepath.Join(filepath.Dir(path), \"credentials.lock\"),\n      \t}, nil\n      }\n  - setFunction name withTimeout, code exactly:\n      // withTimeout is context.WithTimeout with a cancel func that needs no import\n      // at the call site.\n      func withTimeout(ctx context.Context, d time.Duration) (context.Context, func()) {\n      \treturn context.WithTimeout(ctx, d)\n      }\n  - setFunction name withSession, code exactly:\n      // withSession runs fn with a bearer token, refreshing once on a 401. Commands\n      // that need a Provisio session (publish, clone, import) go through it; local\n      // commands never call it.\n      func withSession(ctx context.Context, fn func(bearer string) error) error {\n      \tm, err := sessionManager()\n      \tif err != nil {\n      \t\treturn err\n      \t}\n      \treturn sessionError(m.Do(ctx, fn))\n      }\n\n## Supplementary context\n\nThis section is supplied by the caller, not by the record. It is advisory: it does not add to or change what the record authorized, and the files below remain the only ones the actions may reach.\n\nCaller notes:\n\n# Context for sedum grow (the cmd/provenance CLI and the record package)\n\nPass with: sedum-haiku grow --generators generators --records provenance --prompt-file .sedum/context.md --only <id>\nAdvisory only: behaviour belongs in the record. Editing this file does not regenerate anything.\n\nConventions: cmd/provenance (package main)\n- Package main, cmd/provenance. Every run function is func run<Cmd>(out io.Writer, cmd *cobra.Command, args []string) error and prints through out, never os.Stdout. User-facing errors go through r.fail(format, args...), then return an error.\n- Each import is its own addImport. Write exactly `_, skip := ...` when a binding would otherwise be unused.\n- Generated Go is gofmt-clean and calls only helpers listed here or in the record.\n\nHelpers that exist in package main (call, do not redefine)\n- openRepo(cmd *cobra.Command) (*repo, error); repo has Root string, Config config, Store *record.FilesStore.\n- (r *repo) resolve(id string) (*record.Record, *record.Document, error) prints its own message.\n- (r *repo) recordPath(id) string and versionsDir(id) string (relative to r.Root); const manifestPath; (r *repo) writeManifest() error; author() string; fail(format string, args ...any).\n- (r *repo) git(args ...string) (string, error); commit(message string, paths ...string) error; unstage(paths ...string).\n- snapshotFiles(paths ...string) []fileState; restoreFiles(states []fileState); tag(id string, version int) string gives \"[<id>@<version>]\".\n- recordArg(cmd, args) (string, error) takes the id from --record or the first argument.\n\nRecord library (github.com/livecodelife/provenance/record)\n- Record fields ID, Schema, Status, Version, Title, Intent, Constraints, AffectedScope, ForbiddenScope, Reason, ReasonKind, SealedAtSHA, AssociatedSpecs, Implements, ImplementsVersion.\n- (*Record).ContentHash(specs SpecResolver) (string, []string); (*FilesStore).Specs(), .Versions(id), .Snapshot(id, v), .Save(r, doc), .Load(id), .List().\n- record.Commit(s Store, r *Record, doc *Document, b Bump{Reason, ReasonKind, Author string}) (*Snapshot, error).\n\nConventions: record package\n- Package record (module github.com/livecodelife/provenance). Generated Go is gofmt-clean and calls only helpers listed here or in the record.\n- Canonical encoding is docs/HASHING.md section 5: bytes are written to a *bytes.Buffer; no encoding/json.\n- Each import is its own addImport. Write exactly `_, skip := ...` when a binding would otherwise be unused.\n\nHelpers that exist in package record (call, do not redefine)\n- writeCanonical(b *bytes.Buffer, v any): the encoder switch in hash.go. Its default case panics \"record: non-canonical value type\".\n- writeString(b *bytes.Buffer, s string): a JSON string with only the section 5 escapes.\n- Canonical(v any) string; hashBytes(data []byte) string.\n\nSelections made for this change on an earlier run (context only; they are not applied):\n\n- {\"action\":\"addImport\",\"kwargs\":{\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/session_run.go\",\"path\":\"context\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"addImport\",\"kwargs\":{\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/session_run.go\",\"path\":\"errors\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"addImport\",\"kwargs\":{\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/session_run.go\",\"path\":\"os\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"addImport\",\"kwargs\":{\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/session_run.go\",\"path\":\"path/filepath\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"addImport\",\"kwargs\":{\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/session_run.go\",\"path\":\"time\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"addImport\",\"kwargs\":{\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/session_run.go\",\"path\":\"github.com/livecodelife/provenance/auth\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"setType\",\"kwargs\":{\"code\":\"// exitError carries a process exit status for main to use.\\ntype exitError struct {\\n\\tcode int\\n\\terr  error\\n}\",\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/session_run.go\",\"name\":\"exitError\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"setMethod\",\"kwargs\":{\"code\":\"func (e *exitError) Error() string { return e.err.Error() }\",\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/session_run.go\",\"name\":\"Error\",\"receiver\":\"exitError\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"setMethod\",\"kwargs\":{\"code\":\"func (e *exitError) Unwrap() error { return e.err }\",\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/session_run.go\",\"name\":\"Unwrap\",\"receiver\":\"exitError\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"setFunction\",\"kwargs\":{\"code\":\"// exitCode is the process exit status for err: 3 when a Provisio session is\\n// needed or has expired, 1 for anything else.\\nfunc exitCode(err error) int {\\n\\tvar ee *exitError\\n\\tif errors.As(err, \\u0026ee) {\\n\\t\\treturn ee.code\\n\\t}\\n\\treturn 1\\n}\",\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/session_run.go\",\"name\":\"exitCode\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"setConst\",\"kwargs\":{\"code\":\"const (\\n\\tmsgNeedSession   = \\\"This command needs a Provisio session. Run provenance login (or set PROVISIO_TOKEN in CI).\\\"\\n\\tmsgSessionExpire = \\\"Your Provisio session has expired. Run provenance login.\\\"\\n\\tmsgTokenRejected = \\\"The personal token was rejected (revoked or expired). Replace PROVISIO_TOKEN, or run provenance login.\\\"\\n)\",\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/session_run.go\",\"name\":\"msgNeedSession\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"setFunction\",\"kwargs\":{\"code\":\"// sessionError turns an auth failure into the user-facing message with exit\\n// status 3; other errors pass through unchanged.\\nfunc sessionError(err error) error {\\n\\tswitch {\\n\\tcase err == nil:\\n\\t\\treturn nil\\n\\tcase errors.Is(err, auth.ErrNoSession):\\n\\t\\treturn \\u0026exitError{3, errors.New(msgNeedSession)}\\n\\tcase errors.Is(err, auth.ErrSessionExpired):\\n\\t\\treturn \\u0026exitError{3, errors.New(msgSessionExpire)}\\n\\tcase errors.Is(err, auth.ErrTokenRejected):\\n\\t\\treturn \\u0026exitError{3, errors.New(msgTokenRejected)}\\n\\t}\\n\\treturn err\\n}\",\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/session_run.go\",\"name\":\"sessionError\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"setFunction\",\"kwargs\":{\"code\":\"// serverURL is the auth service for a new sign-in: PROVISIO_AUTH_URL, else the\\n// default. Commands that use a stored sign-in prefer the server it was made on.\\nfunc serverURL() string {\\n\\tif s := os.Getenv(auth.EnvServer); s != \\\"\\\" {\\n\\t\\treturn s\\n\\t}\\n\\treturn auth.DefaultServer\\n}\",\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/session_run.go\",\"name\":\"serverURL\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"setFunction\",\"kwargs\":{\"code\":\"// sessionManager builds the token manager over the default credential store.\\nfunc sessionManager() (*auth.Manager, error) {\\n\\tstore, err := auth.DefaultStore()\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn nil, err\\n\\t}\\n\\tpath, err := auth.DefaultFilePath()\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn nil, err\\n\\t}\\n\\tserver := serverURL()\\n\\tif os.Getenv(auth.EnvServer) == \\\"\\\" \\u0026\\u0026 os.Getenv(auth.EnvToken) == \\\"\\\" {\\n\\t\\tif cred, _, err := store.Load(); err == nil \\u0026\\u0026 cred.Server != \\\"\\\" {\\n\\t\\t\\tserver = cred.Server\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n\\treturn \\u0026auth.Manager{\\n\\t\\tStore:    store,\\n\\t\\tClient:   \\u0026auth.Client{Server: server},\\n\\t\\tLockPath: filepath.Join(filepath.Dir(path), \\\"credentials.lock\\\"),\\n\\t}, nil\\n}\",\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/session_run.go\",\"name\":\"sessionManager\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"setFunction\",\"kwargs\":{\"code\":\"// withTimeout is context.WithTimeout with a cancel func that needs no import\\n// at the call site.\\nfunc withTimeout(ctx context.Context, d time.Duration) (context.Context, func()) {\\n\\treturn context.WithTimeout(ctx, d)\\n}\",\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/session_run.go\",\"name\":\"withTimeout\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"setFunction\",\"kwargs\":{\"code\":\"// withSession runs fn with a bearer token, refreshing once on a 401. Commands\\n// that need a Provisio session (publish, clone, import) go through it; local\\n// commands never call it.\\nfunc withSession(ctx context.Context, fn func(bearer string) error) error {\\n\\tm, err := sessionManager()\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn err\\n\\t}\\n\\treturn sessionError(m.Do(ctx, fn))\\n}\",\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/session_run.go\",\"name\":\"withSession\"}}\n\n## Already present\n\nThese regions already exist in the files below and belong to other changes. Do not select them: an action that resolves to one of them would conflict with the change that owns it.\n\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: describeRoot {\"bin\":\"provenance\"} (owned by prov-2026-76a125e6; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: addShortPersistentFlag:string {\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"flag\":\"config\"} (owned by prov-2026-76a125e6; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: registerCommand {\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"check\"} (owned by prov-2026-063f1395; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: registerCommand {\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"status\"} (owned by prov-2026-12b1ca97; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: registerCommand {\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"deprecate\"} (owned by prov-2026-35439261; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: registerCommand {\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"complete\"} (owned by prov-2026-41fb548c; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: registerCommand {\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"create\"} (owned by prov-2026-44a07768; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: registerCommand {\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"edit\"} (owned by prov-2026-57b8a95b; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: registerCommand {\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"revise\"} (owned by prov-2026-5f69977b; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: registerCommand {\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"open\"} (owned by prov-2026-6db88b75; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: registerCommand {\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"migrate\"} (owned by prov-2026-76a125e6; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: registerCommand {\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"reconcile\"} (owned by prov-2026-9a3aad45; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: registerCommand {\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"repin\"} (owned by prov-2026-9bfa6107; do not select)\n- cmd/proven